  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x7FDD" flags="0x0">
    <title>IGN :: Volt-Dwell - 2</title>
    <description>Ignition coil dwell table -- how long current is allowed to build in the ignition coil primary winding before the spark fires, typically indexed by battery/system voltage and RPM. Governs spark energy; too short = weak spark and misfire risk, too long = coil overheating. Table #1 and #2 likely cover the two coil banks or two dwell stages.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="12" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="1" category="15" />
