  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x2953" flags="0x0">
    <title>Deceleration Fuel Cut</title>
    <description>Decel fuel cut-off (DFCO) table. Defines the RPM/TPS conditions under which the ECU cuts injector fueling entirely on a closed throttle (engine braking) to save fuel and reduce emissions, and the conditions under which fueling resumes. Poorly-tuned DFCO re-engagement is a common cause of decel popping/backfire on modified exhausts.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="2" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="1" category="16" />
